# Line endings
#
# The repository stores every text file with LF. Without this file a Windows
# checkout writes CRLF into the working tree and git reports every file as
# modified, which makes `git diff` useless and corrupts any patch that is
# copied through a Windows tool.
#
# `text=auto` = normalise to LF inside git, check out using the platform's
# native ending. Editors keep working as before; diffs stay clean.
#
# After merging this file, run ONCE:
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "chore: normalise line endings"

* text=auto

# Always LF - these break if they ever get CRLF.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
default.conf    text eol=lf

# Always CRLF - Windows-only tooling.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch, never diff.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.svg           text
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.eot           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.xlsx          binary
*.xls           binary
*.zip           binary
